Subject: Craft by confirmed window clicks, so crafting works on Paper

Applies to: https://github.com/aibengineering/mine-ai-mcp at 2fe1306a0ac51efa99154048e65f2caff00a8934 (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 AI Bengineering; see ../../LICENSE-mine-ai-mcp.txt). Kept by Picasso Lab (UC San Diego) for
"Muse plays Minecraft"; applied by ../../fetch-and-patch.sh with `git apply`.

Why: on Paper 1.21.4 their fork of mineflayer (9fa1140) fails most crafts. After the click that completes a recipe,
Paper answers with a burst (the clicked slot, the result slot empty and then filled, the grid, a full resync) where
vanilla sends one set_slot. craft.js reads the result slot as soon as its click resolves ("Server did not supply the
expected crafting result"), and at a table the resync leaves mineflayer's cursor model wrong, so later clicks put a
stick where a plank belongs.

What: executeCraftPlan crafts through confirmed clicks whenever the bot talks to a real 1.17.1+ server
(src/world/confirmed-window.ts, src/world/confirmed-craft.ts, ported from the agent's src/skills/window.js and
src/skills/craft.js). Every click carries state id -1, which the server always answers with exactly one full resync;
clicks are planned only on a window the server has confirmed (a settle counts the resyncs, then waits for a quiet
spell); the result slot is checked before it is taken; the result is shift-clicked and what arrived is counted. One
window serves the whole plan (the table opens once), and each recipe runs in batches of up to a stack per grid slot
when the outputs fit (the same room rule as the native path, applied per batch). The native per-application path
stays for test doubles without a protocol client and for pre-1.17 servers. Smelting, containers, equip and drop
were measured on Paper and need no change.

